    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0131" n="35" xml:id="pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.62119/98: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dresel</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-11-23T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 23,
                                1921—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>806. With reference to section 9 [<hi rendition="#italic">2</hi>] of Trading with
                    Enemy Act. Please inform me whether “the end of the war” was fixed by
                    President’s peace proclamation. What date shall I state in reply to
                    inquiries?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dresel</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
